Task: The PSQLException duplicate key (user_id, vocabulary_id) is STILL happening. The logs show Hibernate is executing an INSERT statement instead of an UPDATE.

1. Analyze TelegramBotService.java. Find EVERY place where you handle the quiz answer and save to userWordProgressRepository.
2. The bug occurs because the code is still instantiating new UserWordProgress() for existing records. 
3. You MUST rewrite the saving logic using this strict pattern:
   Optional<UserWordProgress> optProgress = userWordProgressRepository.findByAppUserAndVocabulary(appUser, vocabulary);
   UserWordProgress progress;
   if (optProgress.isPresent()) {
       progress = optProgress.get();
   } else {
       progress = new UserWordProgress();
       progress.setAppUser(appUser);
       progress.setVocabulary(vocabulary);
       // set other initial required fields
   }
   // Now update the progress fields (streak, interval, etc.)
   userWordProgressRepository.save(progress);
4. Make sure you don't have multiple conflicting save calls.
5. Apply the patch and set "restartServer": true.